.TH RC.JSON 5 "August 2026" "Cruine 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
rc.json \- Cruine recipe file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rc.json
is the Cruine recipe: a JSON document validated against the
.B RecipeSchema
model. It describes the ROM manifest, the target device and its source
trees, build options, output packaging, patches, and lifecycle hooks.
.PP
Cruine looks for
.B rc.json
in the current working directory. Pass an explicit file with
.BI \-r/\-\-recipe " FILE"
or point the legacy pipeline elsewhere.
.SH TOP-LEVEL KEYS
.TP
.B project_name
(required, string) Short name of the build, e.g.
.BR LineageOS-PocoF3 .
Used for the workspace directory and default archive name.
.TP
.B rom
(required, object) Upstream ROM manifest and build target:
.RS
.TP
.B source
(required, string) Git URL of the manifest, e.g.
.BR https://github.com/LineageOS/android.git .
A
.B file://
URL or plain local path initializes from a local git repository
(fully offline builds).
.TP
.B branch
(required, string) Manifest branch, e.g.
.BR lineage-21.0 .
.TP
.B lunch_prefix
(required, string) Lunch prefix, e.g.
.BR lineage .
.TP
.B build_target
(required, string) Make target, e.g.
.BR bacon .
.TP
.B manifest
(optional, string) Manifest file inside the manifest repository, e.g.
.BR snapshot.xml .
Defaults to
.BR default.xml
or
.BR manifest.xml .
.TP
.B groups
(optional, string) Manifest groups to sync, comma-separated. Defaults to the
.B default
group; prefix a group with
.B -
to exclude it (e.g.
.BR "default,-pdk" ).
.TP
.B depth
(optional, integer) Shallow-clone depth applied to the manifest and every
project (e.g.
.B 1
for a shallow network sync).
.RE
.TP
.B device
(required, object) Target device:
.RS
.TP
.B codename
(required, string) Device codename, e.g.
.BR alioth .
Used to find build outputs under
.IR out/target/product/<codename> .
.TP
.B repositories
(optional, array) Remote source trees. Each entry:
.RS
.TP
.B type
One of
.BR device ,
.BR kernel ,
.BR vendor ,
.BR other .
.TP
.B url
Git URL to clone (a
.B file://
URL or plain local path clones from a local repository).
.TP
.B target_path
Placement inside the workspace, e.g.
.BR device/xiaomi/alioth .
.RE
.TP
.B files
(optional, array) Local source sets instead of git clones. Each entry uses
the same
.BR type / url / target_path
shape, with
.B url
being a local path (copied recursively); a
.B file://
prefix is accepted.
.RE
At least one of
.B repositories
or
.B files
is required.
.TP
.B input
(optional, object) Repack mode: an existing ROM archive to extract, modify,
and re-archive instead of building from source.
.RS
.TP
.B archive
(string, optional) Path (or
.BR file://
path) of the archive to extract.
.TP
.B format
(string, optional) Archive format override; auto-detected from the
extension when omitted. One of
.BR .zip ,
.BR .tar ,
.BR .tar.gz ,
.BR .tar.bz2 ,
.BR .tar.xz ,
.BR .tgz ,
.BR .7z .
.RE
When
.B input.archive
is set, the pipeline extracts the archive into
.IR out/target/product/<codename> ,
runs
.B post_fetch
hooks, patches,
.B pre_build
and
.B post_build
hooks, then packages the result.
.TP
.B options
(optional, object) Build behaviour:
.RS
.TP
.B use_ccache
(boolean, default true) Enable ccache.
.TP
.B ccache_size
(string, default
.BR 50G )
ccache size limit, e.g.
.BR 50G ,
.BR 4G ,
.BR 800M .
.TP
.B clean_build
(boolean, default false) Force
.BR "mka clean" .
.TP
.B build_variant
(string, default
.BR userdebug )
One of
.BR eng ,
.BR user ,
.BR userdebug .
.TP
.B parallel_jobs
(integer, optional) Parallel job count.
.TP
.B extra_make_args
(array of strings, default empty) Extra arguments appended to the
.B mka
invocation.
.RE
.TP
.B output
(optional, object) Packaging:
.RS
.TP
.B format
(string, default
.BR .zip )
One of
.BR .zip ,
.BR .tar.gz ,
.BR .tar.bz2 ,
.BR .tar.xz ,
.BR .tgz ,
.BR .7z ,
.BR .img ,
.BR .iso ,
.BR .tar .
.TP
.B custom_name
(string, optional) Archive basename; defaults to
.IR <project_name>\-<codename> .
.TP
.B compression_level
(integer, 0..9, default 6) Compression level.
.TP
.B exclude_dirs
(array of strings, default
.BR ["obj", "symbols"] )
Directories skipped while packaging.
.RE
.TP
.B patches
(optional, array) Patch files applied after fetch. Each entry:
.RS
.TP
.B file
Path to the patch (a diff readable by
.BR "git apply" ).
.TP
.B directory
Subdirectory of the workspace in which to apply it (default
.BR "." ).
.TP
.B strip
Patch level (default
.BR 1 ).
.RE
.TP
.B hooks
(optional, array) Shell commands run at pipeline phases. Each entry:
.RS
.TP
.B name
Human-readable name.
.TP
.B command
Shell command executed via
.BR sh \-c .
.TP
.B phase
One of
.BR pre_fetch ,
.BR post_fetch ,
.BR pre_build ,
.BR post_build
(default
.BR pre_build ).
.TP
.B workdir
Working directory relative to the workspace (default
.BR "." ).
.RE
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
{
  "project_name": "LineageOS-PocoF3",
  "rom": {
    "source": "https://github.com/LineageOS/android.git",
    "branch": "lineage-21.0",
    "lunch_prefix": "lineage",
    "build_target": "bacon"
  },
  "device": {
    "codename": "alioth",
    "repositories": [
      { "type": "device",
        "url": "https://github.com/LineageOS/android_device_xiaomi_alioth.git",
        "target_path": "device/xiaomi/alioth" },
      { "type": "kernel",
        "url": "https://github.com/LineageOS/android_kernel_xiaomi_alioth.git",
        "target_path": "kernel/xiaomi/alioth" }
    ]
  },
  "options": { "use_ccache": true, "ccache_size": "50G" },
  "output": { "format": ".tar.gz",
              "custom_name": "LineageOS-21.0-alioth-UNOFFICIAL",
              "compression_level": 9 }
}
.fi
.SH REPACK EXAMPLE
.nf
{
  "project_name": "StockMod",
  "rom": {
    "source": "https://example.com/android.git",
    "branch": "b",
    "lunch_prefix": "lineage",
    "build_target": "bacon"
  },
  "device": { "codename": "alioth",
              "repositories": [ ] },
  "input": { "archive": "/srv/roms/stock.zip" },
  "options": { "use_ccache": false },
  "output": { "format": ".zip" },
  "hooks": [
    { "name": "debloat",
      "command": "rm -f out/target/product/alioth/system/app/News/News.apk",
      "phase": "post_build" }
  ]
}
.fi
.SH GENERATING
A starter recipe is produced with:
.PP
.nf
cru init [target]
cru --generate-template ./rc.json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cru (1),
.BR crush (1)
